@ 29.1.1.1.41 - Proto-Athabaskan to Northern Tutchone
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85 Most stem-final consonants lost, though some plain and labialized palatal reflexes have developed differently Acquisition of nasalized vowels and diphthongs /o/ somehow develops
	TS {TŠ,TŠʷ} > TH TS
	[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo] > TŠ (although /xʲ/ remained as such in a few dialect͡s)
	Q > [+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo]
	{ɑ,ə,ʊ} > {a,o}
	Vˀ > V:[+high tone]